## Explorer: entity-type filter no longer recounts the graph on open
Context: Landed on 0.9.0 (PR #189 was opened against master/0.8.1). The
Knowledge Graph Explorer's Filter panel filled its entity-type list from
/dtwin/sync/stats?refresh=true. The refresh flag bypasses the stats cache,
so every open recomputed all graph aggregates (total, distinct subjects,
type and predicate distributions) over the whole triple store. On a
20.8M-triple Lakebase graph the list stayed on "Loading types..." for a
long time.
Changes:
1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   _populateFilterEntityTypes fills the list from the loaded ontology first
   (new _ontologyEntityTypes, a read of /ontology/get-loaded-ontology), then
   narrows it to the types with instances from /dtwin/sync/stats without
   refresh. The stats cache is cleared at the start of every build, so the
   cached list matches the current graph. _renderStatsDropdown keeps the
   user's selection when the list is re-rendered.
Tests added:
- tests/units/front/test_explorer_type_dropdown.py: the type list does not
  bypass the stats cache, reads the cached stats, fills from the ontology
  first, and keeps the selection on re-render.
Modified files:
- src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
- tests/units/front/test_explorer_type_dropdown.py
